; $.SCREEN: &2800 bytes at sector &03E. The loading picture - a space
; station, planets and the "pipeline" logo over the Superior Software and
; Acornsoft logos - as a MODE 5 screen: the whole of screen memory from &5800
; to &7FFF, saved as it stood (docs/img/loading-screen.png, or render it with
; `tools/beebscreen.py 5 data/screen.bin OUT.png --palette 0,1,3,5`).
;
; MENU *LOADs it straight into screen memory first thing (line 250: MODE 5,
; cursor off, VDU 19,3,5 to make colour 3 magenta), so the palette is black,
; red, yellow, magenta; it stays up for ten seconds or until a key
; (INKEY(1000)). *LOAD runs nothing, so the catalogued exec address is
; unused.
;
; Layout is the MOS's for MODE 5: 32 character rows of 320 bytes, each row
; 40 cells of 8 bytes, one byte per pixel line of the cell; a byte is 4
; pixels, pixel p's colour taking bit 7-p as its high bit and bit 3-p as its
; low. The picture fills the top 27 character rows; the last five are blank.

SCREEN_MODE5 = &5800
SCREEN_END = &8000
MODE5_ROW_BYTES = 320

SECTION screen, filename="SCREEN", org=SCREEN_MODE5, load=&5800, exec=&5800
.loading_picture
    INCBIN "../data/screen.bin"
    ASSERT P% = SCREEN_MODE5 + 27 * MODE5_ROW_BYTES
.blank_rows
    SKIPTO SCREEN_END
ENDSECTION
